<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.11.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01060</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.11.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bb54ac74-2064-460c-8dbf-2e230c3f82b7</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="548dcd73-d585-4139-a459-d6bf8980d9fe" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 1 - 3, use the graph below.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="This graph shows four functions on an x, y coordinate plane. The \(x\)-axis runs from negative 8 to 9. The \(y\)-axis runs from negative 8 to 8.  The first shows the decreasing function h of x = negative 2 times x plus 2. It passes through the points (0, 2) and (1, 0). The second is an increasing function that shows f of x = 2 times x plus 3. It passes through the points (0, 3) and (-1.5, 0). The third is an increasing function that shows j of x = 2 times x minus 6 and passes through the points (0, -6) and (3, 0). The fourth line is an increasing function where g of x = x divided by 2 minus 4 and passes through the points (0, -4) and (2 ,0).">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_14_16_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
            <para>Tell the shift from \(j(x)=2x-6\) to \(f(x)=2x+3\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>Down 3</para>
            <para>Down 8</para>
            <para>Up 9</para>
            <para>Up 8</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Up 9</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.11.2. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is up 9. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="5eae2be9-0274-4a58-9340-3bca315b5440" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Tell the transformations from \(f(x)=2x+3\) to \(h(x)=-2x+2\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>Vertical reflection, up 1</para>
            <para>Vertical reflection, down 1</para>
            <para>Vertical stretch, right 1</para>
            <para>Vertical stretch, left 1</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Vertical reflection, down 1</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is vertical reflection, down 1. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="0086830d-c6d4-4fca-b4c6-9e78332d2635" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Describe the transformations made from the parent linear function to achieve \(g(x)=\frac12 x -4\).
          <emphasis>Select two</emphasis> that apply:
        </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Vertical compression of \(\frac12\); Down 4</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4. </para>
            <para>The correct answers are vertical compression of \(\frac12\), down 4. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="d22bcd2b-aa35-487b-8ddf-30111943cf25" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="This graph shows two lines on an x, y coordinate plane. The \(x\)-axis runs from negative 4 to 6. The \(y\)-axis runs from negative 3 to 8.  The first line has the equation y = -3 times x divided by 2 plus 1.  The second line has the equation y = -3 times x divided by 2 plus 7.  The lines do not cross.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_14_16_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
              <para>What are the equations of the two lines shown? <emphasis>Select two </emphasis>that apply:</para>
            </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(y=-\frac32x+1\) and \(y=-\frac32x+7\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.11.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \(y=-\frac32x+1\) and \(y=-\frac32x+7\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="356feacc-af8e-4824-9fa8-1fa282e2d1f4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The linear function \(f(x)=x\) has a vertical stretch of 3, a vertical reflection, and a vertical shift down 4. Which of the following is the new function?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=3x+4\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=-3x+4\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=3x-4\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=-3x-4\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(x)=-3x-4\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=-3x-4\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="90cae9a1-c577-4ffa-a698-0752ff5525af" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The linear function \(f(x)=x\) has a vertical compression of \(\frac13\) and a vertical shift up 2. Which of the following is the new function?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=\frac13x+2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=-\frac13x+2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=2x+\frac13\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=2x-\frac13\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(x)=\frac13x+2\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=\frac13x+2\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="23cd6648-507a-4211-b236-f0868aca4911" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>What is the equation of the function graphed?
          <para><figure><media alt="This graph shows a linear function graphed on an x y coordinate plane. The x axis is labeled from negative 2 to 8 and the y axis is labeled from negative 1 to 8. The function f is graph along the points (0, 7) and (4, 4)."><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_14_16_03.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
        </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=3x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(y=\frac34x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-\frac34x+7\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-\frac43x+7\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(y=-\frac34x+7\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.1 – 4.11.4. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=-\frac34x+7\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="a257dca8-2c02-47e2-bc99-3ccbffc3ed08" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The linear function \(f(x)=x\) has a vertical compression of \(\frac13\) and a vertical shift down 2. Which of the following is the new function?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=\frac13x -2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=-\frac13x-2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=2x+\frac13\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=2x - \frac13\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(x)=\frac13x -2\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 – 4.11.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=\frac13x -2\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="67af96c8-1a0c-4c07-9b8b-a709e7d55dbb" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which two transformations can be used to obtain the graph of \(g(x) = -(x-c)\) from the graph of \(g(x) = x\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>A translation to the right \(c\) units followed by a reflection across the \(x\)-axis</para>
            <para>A translation to the left \(c\) units followed by a reflection across the \(x\)-axis</para>
            <para>A translation to the right \(c\) units followed by a reflection across the \(y\)-axis</para>
            <para>A translation to the left \(c\) units followed by a reflection across the \(y\)-axis</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! A translation to the right \(c\) units followed by a reflection across the \(x\)-axis.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.11.2 and 4.11.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: A translation to the right \(c\) units followed by a reflection across the \(x\)-axis.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="a458c908-a4d6-4aaa-8e32-532cf9418259" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For the functions \(h\) and \(g\), which statement is true if \(h(x) = g(x + 14) - 12\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>The graph of \(h\) is the result of the graph of \(g\) being translated right 14 units and down 12 units.</para>
            <para>The graph of \(h\) is the result of the graph of \(g\) being translated left 14 units and down 12 units.</para>
            <para>The graph of \(h\) is the result of the graph of \(g\) being translated right 14 units and up 12 units.</para>
            <para>The graph of \(h\) is the result of the graph of \(g\) being translated left 14 units and up 12 units.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The graph of \(h\) is the result of the graph of \(g\) being translated left 14 units and down 12 units.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.11.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: The graph of \(h\) is the result of the graph of \(g\) being translated left 14 units and down 12 units.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="14fc61a9-cead-4fcb-b070-e24a7df09970" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which type of transformation can be used to obtain the graph of \(g(x) = 4(2 + x)\) from the graph of \(f(x) = 2+x\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>Vertical shrink or compression</para>
            <para>Vertical shift down</para>
            <para>Vertical shift up</para>
            <para>Vertical stretch</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The correct transformation is a vertical stretch.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.11.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: vertical stretch.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
